| editorial =
'''The bond that breaks in public'''

The Kuroshio bond broke tonight. Not in a ring — in a ring is where bonds are supposed to break. In a ring is where the break is honest. KAZUKI and Leoni were forced to team. They won by disqualification. The tension was visible after the bell. The audience saw it. The audience paid to see it.

NOPW is a story told in a ring. The story is the bond. The break is the drama. The Island Invasion Tour is August 9 — Fangatapu, Vaiahi, 12,000 people on a beach. The question is whether the bond holds or shatters. That is the story. That is what the audience buys.

The Kuroshio bond is not a real bond. It is a story about a bond. But the story is real. The audience's investment is real. The tension is real. The break — when it comes — will be real. That is the art. That is the business. The art and the business are the same thing.

